{
  "about": "A text field's context menu, the platform's for every React Native TextInput (docs/adr/0037-text-editing.mdx; sample/TextMenuProbe.tsx: a Bloom field, a plain TextInput, a secure field; sample/oxyos/text-menu.js), with a second application beside it (`companion`) that must receive nothing. A secondary click or a Control-click focuses the field, selects the word under the pointer unless the click is within the selection (the caret off a word, nothing in a secure field) and opens Bloom's ContextMenu in the platform's popup at the pointer, announced as a menu, its rows enabled as they apply (Undo and Redo with the field's history, Cut and Copy with a selection outside a secure field, Paste with text on the clipboard, Select All with text); the keys move past disabled rows, Return and a press choose, Escape closes, and the field keeps its focus and selection, the keyboard back on it. Each step checks the text and selection React receives, exactly the React events, focus, the field the compositor holds and the clipboard.",
  "module": "TextMenuProbe",
  "window": [
    640,
    360
  ],
  "locale": "es_ES.UTF-8",
  "companion": {
    "module": "DropProbe",
    "window": [
      260,
      180
    ],
    "at": [
      980,
      200
    ]
  },
  "final": {
    "focus_input": "line"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "name": "the window made active by a press on nothing in it: no field has focus",
      "do": [
        "press",
        [
          500,
          300
        ]
      ],
      "allow_unchanged": true,
      "expect": {
        "popups": 0,
        "react": {
          "touchStart@RootView#1": 1,
          "touchEnd@RootView#1": 1
        },
        "delivered": {
          "1": {
            "focus.in": 1,
            "enter": 1,
            "press": 1,
            "release": 1
          },
          "companion": {
            "focus.out": 1
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a secondary click on \"mundo\" in the Bloom field, which has no focus: the field takes focus with the word selected, as on a Mac, and its context menu opens at the pointer in a popup, announced as a menu, Undo and Redo disabled (nothing to undo) and Paste too (the clipboard is empty)",
      "do": [
        "press_secondary",
        [
          95,
          42
        ]
      ],
      "expect": {
        "texts": [
          "Line: \"Hola mundo café\" [5,10]"
        ],
        "popups": 1,
        "focus_input": "line",
        "react": {
          "focus@line": 1,
          "selectionChange@line": 1,
          "oxyosTextMenu@line": 1
        },
        "at": {
          "popup": [
            {
              "role": "Menu",
              "name": "Menú contextual"
            },
            {
              "role": "MenuItem",
              "name": "Deshacer",
              "state": [
                "disabled",
                "focused"
              ]
            },
            {
              "role": "MenuItem",
              "name": "Rehacer",
              "state": [
                "disabled"
              ]
            },
            {
              "role": "MenuItem",
              "name": "Cortar"
            },
            {
              "role": "MenuItem",
              "name": "Copiar"
            },
            {
              "role": "MenuItem",
              "name": "Pegar",
              "state": [
                "disabled"
              ]
            },
            {
              "role": "MenuItem",
              "name": "Seleccionar todo"
            }
          ]
        },
        "delivered": {
          "1": {
            "focus.out": 1,
            "leave": 1,
            "press": 1,
            "release": 1
          },
          "2": {
            "focus.in": 1
          },
          "companion": {}
        }
      }
    },
    {
